# File

Standard library for file I/O operations.

## Note
Reads a whole file into Text.

## To native read (path: Text) -> Result of Text and Text

## Note
Writes Text to a file, replacing its contents.

## To native write (path: Text) and (content: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text

## Note
Adds Text to the end of a file, creating the file when it is absent.

The directory it is in must already exist — `makeDirs` makes it. A log or a ledger written one entry
at a time appends, so an entry already written is never rewritten.

## To native appendFile (path: Text) and (content: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text

## Note
Whether anything — a file or a directory — is at a path.

## To native fileExists (path: Text) -> Bool

## Note
The names of the entries in a directory, sorted, without `.` and `..` — names, not paths: join one
to the directory to reach it.

## To native listDir (path: Text) -> Result of Seq of Text and Text

## Note
Makes a directory and every missing directory above it. One that already exists is not an error,
so a program can call this before every write into it; a file in the way is.

## To native makeDirs (path: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text

## Note
Renames a file, replacing whatever was at the new name.

On one file system the rename is atomic: write the new content to a temporary name beside the file,
then rename it over the file, and a reader sees either the old content or the new, never half of one.

## To native renameFile (from: Text) and (to: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text
